2026-11-18 Chat scroll generation boundary

Baseline: a short drag after generation snapped back to offset 0 on both Flutter platform variants. Chrome also reproduced a pending near-bottom window snapping the conversation after generation had completed.

Final: Flutter chat view and sheet suites passed all 93 cases (reporter elapsed time about 6 seconds). Browser fixture passed all 8 cases, including completion during the resume window, idle wheel scrolling, JIT opening of a finished conversation at the bottom, and another send from the bottom or history. The explicit jump button still works after generation completes.

TypeScript and Vite production build passed. Vite reported 2.43 seconds.
Flutter and Chrome used local conversation fixtures. No live network streaming, model tokens, or API costs. Device latency and physical gestures were not measured.
